  "logline": "Over the last 75 years, eleven mayors governed New York City. Each inherited a crisis -- or created one. This sprawling investigation traces the policy decisions, power grabs, incompetence, and ideology that transformed America's greatest city from the safe, prosperous 1950s into a modern cautionary tale.",
  "detail": "A street-level history of power in New York. Archival footage, on-the-ground reporting, and candid voices from the neighborhoods that lived through each administration.",
